# sweep: --bare
# A refreshed brief keeps its stories for reading offline, keeps going when
# the app is put in the background, survives a restart, and a refresh with no
# network leaves the saved brief in place with a way to try again.
wait-for Nothing yet
tap Refresh
# Leaving mid-refresh does not stop it; the brief is there on return.
lifecycle background
wait 3000
lifecycle foreground
wait-for as of
wait-idle 60000
wait-for Ready offline:
expect Top stories
expect 1 of
clean
shot brief-ready
tap-id story-0
wait-idle 30000
expect-missing Daily brief
clean
shot story
page next
wait-idle
page next
wait-idle
tap Back
wait-for Daily brief
expect 1 of
tap-id next
wait-for 2 of
clean
shot brief-page-2
tap-id previous
wait-for 1 of
# Stories still arriving over the live network finish before the restart.
wait-idle 30000
restart
wait-for as of
expect Ready offline:
# With the network gone a saved story still opens.
scenario offline
tap-id story-0
wait-idle 30000
expect-missing Daily brief
expect-missing could not be opened
clean
shot story-offline
tap Back
wait-for Daily brief
tap Refresh
wait-idle 30000
wait-for The brief below is the one already saved
expect fetched
expect Try again
expect Ready offline:
clean
shot refresh-offline
scenario normal
# Refreshing over a saved brief draws its progress under the list, and the
# whole screen must still fit the panel.
tap Try again
wait-idle 60000
wait-for as of
expect-missing already saved
